WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:05.717
Step nine plans the Service Health alerts
at the production management group:

2
00:00:05.717 --> 00:00:10.425
two steps, assign and remediate, each
would apply, and a plan SHA-256.

3
00:00:10.425 --> 00:00:13.000
It's the same plan as Module 2's.

4
00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:17.737
Step ten plans production's rollback,
in reverse order of the deployment.

5
00:00:17.737 --> 00:00:21.013
First, unregister the
weekly scheduled task.

6
00:00:21.013 --> 00:00:23.537
Second, delete the policy assignment.

7
00:00:23.537 --> 00:00:28.012
Third, a manual step: list the resource
group the remediation created,

8
00:00:28.012 --> 00:00:33.350
because the change record decides on what
the remediation created, not the script.

9
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:35.437
Dry run: nothing changed.

10
00:00:35.437 --> 00:00:38.303
Then the second command
tries to apply that

11
00:00:38.303 --> 00:00:41.088
plan with a hash nobody
approved, all zeros.

12
00:00:41.088 --> 00:00:44.427
It's refused: the approved hash must match

13
00:00:44.427 --> 00:00:48.062
the plan's SHA-256 before
apply runs anything.

14
00:00:48.062 --> 00:00:51.100
That's the guard against a
plan changed after approval.

15
00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:55.148
Step eleven runs the deploy
scripts' tests: twenty-five pass,

16
00:00:55.148 --> 00:01:00.188
none fail and none are skipped, on Windows,
where one of them runs only there.

17
00:01:00.188 --> 00:01:02.470
Then delete the dry run's folders.
